{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>לרעות את.</b> Rashi explained: <b>את</b> is dotted — they went only to graze themselves. It is as though <b>את</b> is crossed out, meaning not all the flocks — for example, 'they shall graze בשן' etc., and it is not written 'they shall graze את בשן ואת גלעד.' But if you interpret the word <b>את</b>, it implies they went to graze the flock in a grazing place. Another interpretation: <b>לרעות את</b> themselves along with their father's sheep — for in every expression of grazing livestock you will find <b>את</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:42.031678665Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}